Description: seaf-fsck.sh: use this packaging's fixed FHS paths, add a
 running-check before repairing the object store, require the seafile identity
 Same TOPDIR-detection problem as reset-admin.sh (see reset-admin-fhs-paths.patch);
 sources /etc/seafile/seafile.env instead. Unlike upstream's seaf-gc.sh, this
 script had no guard against running concurrently with the live daemons - added
 one (same validate_already_running as the patched seaf-gc.sh: checks
 systemctl unit state for seafile.service, seafile-fileserver.service,
 seahub.service and seafile-fuse.service), since --repair mutates the object
 store just as gc does. Re-execs as the seafile user via runuser when invoked
 as anyone else, before doing anything, for the same file-ownership reason as
 seaf-gc.sh.
Author: dionysius <dragon.dionysius@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Comment: install-layout specific, not something upstream's own tar.gz/docker install needs.
